.TH HD-UP 1 "October 2026" "hd-base" "HyprDebian"
.SH NAME
hd-up \- upgrade the system after a ZFS snapshot
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B hd-up
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B hd-up
upgrades the system with
.BR apt (8),
after a snapshot of the root dataset, so an upgrade that went wrong can be
undone with
.BR "zfs rollback" .
.IP 1. 4
It updates the package lists.
.IP 2. 4
It shows the packages that can be upgraded, and stops when there are none.
.IP 3. 4
It asks whether to go on; anything but
.B y
stops it.
.IP 4. 4
It takes the snapshot
.BI rpool/hyprdebian@hd-up- date _ time\fR,
such as
.BR rpool/hyprdebian@hd-up-2026-10-17_143000 ,
and stops when that fails.
.IP 5. 4
It runs
.BR "apt full-upgrade" ,
so upgrades that need new packages or remove old ones are not held back.
.PP
Run it as a user who may use
.BR sudo (8),
or as root.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show a short help and exit.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 when the system is up to date or the upgrade was cancelled, otherwise the
exit status of the command that failed.
.SH EXAMPLES
Undo the last upgrade, after a reboot into a system that still works, or
from a live system:
.PP
.RS
.nf
zfs list \-t snapshot rpool/hyprdebian
zfs rollback rpool/hyprdebian@hd\-up\-2026\-10\-17_143000
.fi
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR hd-base (7),
.BR apt (8),
.BR zfs-rollback (8)
.SH AUTHOR
Erik Van Hamme <erik.vanhamme@gmail.com>
